# File Organization

## Folder structure (adapt to your stack)
- `src/` — source code only
- `src/features/` — feature-based modules (preferred over type-based grouping)
- `src/components/` — reusable, generic UI components
- `src/lib/` — shared utilities and helpers
- `src/hooks/` — custom hooks (React) or composables (Vue)
- `src/types/` — shared types/interfaces
- `src/locales/` — i18n translation files
- `src/services/` — API clients, external integrations
- `tests/` — integration/e2e tests (co-locate unit tests with source)
- `docs/` — markdown documentation
- `scripts/` — build, dev, deploy scripts

## Naming conventions
- Files: `kebab-case.ts` (e.g. `user-profile.tsx`)
- Components: `PascalCase` exports (`export function UserProfile()`)
- Functions/variables: `camelCase`
- Constants: `SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE`
- Types/Interfaces: `PascalCase`
- Boolean variables: `is`, `has`, `should`, `can` prefix

## Hard rules
- ONE primary export per file
- NO files at project root except config (`package.json`, `tsconfig.json`, etc.)
- NO generic dumping grounds: forbidden names → `utils.ts`, `helpers.ts`, `misc.ts`, `common.ts`. Use specific names like `date-formatting.ts`, `string-validators.ts`.
- Files MUST be under 300 lines. Refactor if exceeded.
- Folders MUST contain at least 2 files (or have a clear plan to grow). No single-file folders.

## When creating new files
- First search the codebase for similar existing code — extend before creating
- New top-level folders require explicit justification
- Place file next to its closest relative, not in a generic bucket
